    "content": "{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <cstdio>\\n#include <algorithm>\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n#include <omp.h>\\n#endif\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n, s;\\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\\n    \\n    // Read matrix as flat vector for better cache locality (optional)\\n    std::vector<std::vector<int>> mat(n, std::vector<int>(n));\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\\n            scanf(\\\"%d\\\", &mat[i][j]);\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    // Step 1: Compute vertical prefix sums per column.\\n    // vPref[j][r] = sum of mat[0..r][j]\\n    std::vector<std::vector<int>> vPref(n, std::vector<int>(n));\\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\\n        int cum = 0;\\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\\n            cum += mat[i][j];\\n            vPref[j][i] = cum;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    // Step 2: Search all starting rows in parallel.\\n    int mxSum = 0;\\n    #pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(static)\\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n - s; ++i) {\\n        long long curSum = 0;\\n        // Initial sum of submatrix at (i,0): columns 0..s-1\\n        int bottomRow = i + s - 1;\\n        int topMinusOne = i > 0 ? vPref[0][i-1] : 0; // not used yet\\n        for (int j = 0; j < s; ++j) {\\n            int colSum = vPref[j][bottomRow];\\n            if (i > 0) colSum -= vPref[j][i-1];\\n            curSum += colSum;\\n        }\\n        mxSum = std::max(mxSum, static_cast<int>(curSum));\\n\\n        // Slide horizontally across columns\\n        for (int j = s; j < n; ++j) {\\n            int leftCol = vPref[j - s][bottomRow];\\n            if (i > 0) leftCol -= vPref[j - s][i-1];\\n            curSum -= leftCol;\\n\\n            int rightCol = vPref[j][bottomRow];\\n            if (i > 0) rightCol -= vPref[j][i-1];\\n            curSum += rightCol;\\n\\n            mxSum = std::max(mxSum, static_cast<int>(curSum));\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    printf(\\\"%d\\\\n\\\", mxSum);\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Parallelize submatrix maximum sum using vertical prefix sums for column-wise cumulative sums computed in parallel (static schedule), then search all starting rows with independent horizontal sliding windows, each thread handling a contiguous range of rows via #pragma omp parallel for reduction(max) schedule(static). This demonstrates OpenMP work sharing (parallel for on both construction and search), reductions (max reduction), explicit scheduling control (static schedule to minimize overhead), and thread granularity through per-row workload.\",\n  \"notes\": \"Uses vertical prefix sums precomputed in O(N^2) with static parallelization. The main search loop is embarrassingly parallel over starting rows, each performing a sliding window horizontally. Reduction(max) combines results. Static scheduling avoids dynamic overhead since iterations have equal work (O(n-s+1) per row). Memory: two n×n int arrays (~512 MB for n=8000), acceptable on target system.\",\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Add vertical prefix sum precomputation with #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\",\n    \"Replace sequential snake traversal with independent row-parallel sliding window using #pragma omp parallel for reduction(max) schedule(static)\"\n  ]\n}",
